$path = "d:\DATA LAPTOP LAMA\Upi\Personal Finance Tracker\Personal-Finance-Tracker\.kiro\specs\personal-finance-tracker\requirements.md"
$text = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllText($path, [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8)

$markerText = "## Requirement Coverage Matrix (Phase 15+)"
$idx = $text.IndexOf($markerText)

if ($idx -lt 0) {
    Write-Error "Marker not found!"
    exit 1
}

$before = $text.Substring(0, $idx)

$insertion = "### Requirement 23 - Local Data Migration`n`nThe application SHALL provide a controlled, explicit, and reversible migration path for`nauthenticated users who have existing financial data in LocalStorage and wish to move it to`nthe Supabase cloud store.`n`n#### 23.1 Migration Detection`n`nWHEN a user authenticates, THE App SHALL detect whether the user's browser contains LocalStorage`nfinancial data under the key ``financeTrackerData``. THE App SHALL also determine whether cloud data`nalready exists for that user in the Supabase ``transactions`` table. THE App SHALL use this`ninformation to classify the migration scenario and determine whether a migration opportunity`nshould be offered.`n`n#### 23.2 Explicit User Consent`n`nTHE App SHALL NOT silently upload LocalStorage data to the cloud at any time. Migration SHALL`nonly proceed after the user has been informed about the presence of local data and has`nexplicitly initiated the import action. Signing in alone SHALL NOT trigger migration.`n`n#### 23.3 Pre-Migration Validation`n`nWHEN the user initiates migration, THE App SHALL validate every local transaction, every local`ncustom category, and the local settings before any upload begins.`n`nTransaction validation SHALL verify: the ``id`` field is a non-blank string; the ``type`` field`nis exactly ``income`` or ``expense``; the ``itemName`` field is non-blank after trimming; the ``amount```nis a finite number greater than 0; the ``category`` field is non-blank after trimming; the ``date```nfield matches the format ``YYYY-MM-DD`` and represents a valid calendar date; the ``createdAt```nfield is a non-blank string.`n`nCustom category validation SHALL verify: the ``name`` is non-blank after trimming; the ``type```nis ``income`` or ``expense``; no duplicate ``(name, type)`` pair exists in the local custom category`nlist; the name is not a member of the built-in default category sets.`n`nSettings validation SHALL verify: the ``currency`` value exists and is a member of`n``Supported_Currencies``.`n`nIF any records fail validation, THE App SHALL report the invalid records to the user and SHALL`nNOT silently upload them. The user SHALL be given the opportunity to review invalid records`nbefore deciding whether to proceed with migrating the valid subset.`n`n#### 23.4 Transaction Idempotency`n`nTHE migration SHALL use each transaction's existing ``id`` value as the cloud record's primary key.`n`nIF a transaction with the same ``id`` does not exist in the cloud, THE App SHALL insert it.`n`nIF a transaction with the same ``id`` already exists in the cloud AND the record data is`nidentical, THE App SHALL skip it without error.`n`nIF a transaction with the same ``id`` already exists in the cloud AND the record data differs`nin any field, THE App SHALL NOT silently overwrite the cloud record. THE App SHALL report the`nconflict to the user.`n`nIF the cloud contains transactions that are not present in LocalStorage, THE App SHALL NOT`ndelete them.`n`n#### 23.5 Category Handling`n`nDefault categories (Food, Transport, Fun, Bills, Shopping, Health, Other for expense; Salary,`nFreelance, Business, Investment, Gift, Other for income) SHALL NOT be inserted into the cloud`n``categories`` table. These are JavaScript constants and do not require cloud persistence.`n`nWHEN migrating a custom category, IF a category with the same ``name`` and ``type`` already exists`nin the cloud for the authenticated user, THE App SHALL skip it without error. Only non-default`ncustom categories that do not already exist in the cloud SHALL be inserted.`n`n#### 23.6 Settings and Currency Handling`n`nWHEN local settings and cloud settings contain the same ``currency`` value, THE App SHALL migrate`nthe currency setting without prompting the user.`n`nWHEN local settings and cloud settings contain different ``currency`` values, THE App SHALL present`nboth values to the user and require the user to explicitly choose which currency to keep. THE App`nSHALL NOT apply either value automatically without user confirmation. THE App SHALL NOT perform`nany exchange-rate conversion on any transaction amount under any circumstances.`n`n#### 23.7 Existing Cloud Data Scenarios`n`nTHE App SHALL define the following behaviors for each migration scenario:`n`n- **Scenario A** (local data present, cloud empty): Migration is available. The App SHALL offer`n  to import all valid local records to the cloud.`n- **Scenario B** (local empty, cloud has data): No migration is needed. The App SHALL NOT prompt`n  the user.`n- **Scenario C** (both local and cloud have data with no overlapping IDs): Migration is available.`n  The App SHALL merge local records into the cloud without deleting existing cloud records.`n- **Scenario D** (both contain records with identical IDs and data): Migration is available but`n  all records will be skipped as duplicates. Migration completes with zero insertions. Verification`n  SHALL still confirm cloud records are present.`n- **Scenario E** (both contain records with the same IDs but differing data): The App SHALL report`n  each conflicting record to the user. Non-conflicting records SHALL still be migrated. Conflicting`n  records SHALL NOT be inserted or overwritten without explicit user action.`n`n#### 23.8 Partial Migration and Retry`n`nIF migration fails partway through due to a network error or other interruption, THE App SHALL`nallow the user to retry the migration.`n`nWHEN retrying, THE App SHALL skip any records that were already successfully uploaded in a prior`nattempt, using the migration progress marker to determine which records were previously completed.`nThis retry behavior SHALL ensure that retrying does not create duplicate cloud records.`n`nTHE App SHALL NOT mark migration as successfully completed until all records have been uploaded`nand verified.`n`n#### 23.9 Migration Verification`n`nAFTER uploading all records, THE App SHALL verify the migration by fetching the uploaded records`nfrom the cloud and comparing them against the migration manifest. Verification SHALL check:`n`n- All migrated transaction IDs are present in the cloud.`n- All migrated custom category ``(name, type)`` pairs are present in the cloud.`n- The cloud settings ``currency`` matches the expected value.`n- A representative sample of migrated records has field values (amount, type, itemName) that`n  match the local source records.`n`nVerification SHALL NOT rely on count alone. THE App SHALL NOT set migration status to`n``completed`` until all verification checks pass.`n`n#### 23.10 LocalStorage Preservation`n`nLocalStorage financial data SHALL NOT be deleted before migration has been verified as`nsuccessfully completed. EVEN AFTER successful verification, THE App SHALL preserve the`nLocalStorage financial data as a backup unless the user explicitly chooses to clear it.`nTHE App SHALL provide a `"Clear local data`" action that is only available after verification`nreturns a successful result.`n`n#### 23.11 Migration Status Tracking`n`nTHE App SHALL maintain a migration status for each authenticated user. The valid status values`nare: ``not-needed``, ``available``, ``validating``, ``ready``, ``in-progress``, ``partial``, ``completed``,`n``failed``.`n`nMigration status SHALL be stored in the browser's LocalStorage under the key`n``financeTrackerMigration_`${userId}``, where ``userId`` is the authenticated user's immutable`nSupabase UUID. THE App SHALL NOT use the user's email address as part of the status key.`nThis key SHALL NOT be readable by other users.`n`n#### 23.12 Security`n`nTHE migration SHALL use only the authenticated user's Supabase ``user.id`` (immutable UUID) as`nthe ownership key for all uploaded records. THE App SHALL NOT use email address, username, or`ndisplay name as an ownership identifier for migrated records.`n`nTHE migration SHALL NOT use service-role credentials or any privileged API that bypasses`nRow-Level Security. All migrated records SHALL have their ``user_id`` field set to the`nauthenticated user's UUID. Row-Level Security policies SHALL remain the database-level`nenforcement boundary for all migrated data.`n`n#### 23.13 Offline and Network Behavior`n`nIF the user is authenticated but the network is unavailable when migration is initiated, THE`nApp SHALL not attempt migration and SHALL inform the user that a network connection is required.`n`nIF migration has started and the network becomes unavailable during the migration, THE App SHALL`nstop further upload attempts, preserve LocalStorage intact, set migration status to ``partial``,`nand allow the user to retry when the network is restored.`n`n---`n`n## Requirement Coverage Matrix (Phase 15+)`n`n| Requirement | Description                        | Phase(s)    | Status         |`n|-------------|------------------------------------|-------------|----------------|`n| 1-18        | Original v1 Finance Tracker        | Phase 1-14  | Implemented    |`n| 19          | Authentication                     | Phase 15    | In progress    |`n| 20          | User Identity & Data Isolation     | Phase 16    | Not implemented |`n| 21          | Local Data Migration               | Phase 17    | Not implemented |`n| 22          | Authentication Privacy & Security  | Phase 15-18 | In progress    |`n| 23          | Local Data Migration (detailed)    | Phase 17    | Not implemented |`n"

$newContent = $before + $insertion
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($path, $newContent, [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8)
Write-Host "SUCCESS. New file length: $($newContent.Length)"
